 "assignment_note": "Which photograph fills which slot in the cut. Chosen for MAXIMUM DISTINCTNESS as well as headcount: the first selection took the three biggest crowds (002, 003, 004) and they turned out to be three frames of the same overhead photo seconds apart -- on screen, one image shown three times. 002 is the overhead wide of the whole summit and takes the longest hold; the rest are ground-level crowds from the same minute, so the six still read as one set. Pairwise correlation peaks at 0.27 against the 0.42-0.57 of the rejected trio. Owner-rejected on the wider set: summit-11 (one person), summit-03 (its near-duplicate), summit-15 (blurred audience). act1_title_cover is the megacut's act I title cover (owner, 2026-08-15: '2:14 remove the comic book cover for this segment and use a group picture from kubecon contributor summit'): group-007 picked because it fills 16:9 with people -- two dozen faces, front row sharp, badges legible -- and its worst pairwise correlation against the six below is 0.18, under the limit.",
